PPRREEVVEENNTT CCHHAANNGGEESS FFOORR AA PPAACCKKAAGGEE
       hhoolldd
           hold is used to mark a package as held back, which will prevent the
           package from being automatically installed, upgraded or removed.

       uunnhhoolldd
           unhold is used to cancel a previously set hold on a package to
           allow all actions again.

       sshhoowwhhoolldd
           showhold is used to print a list of packages on hold in the same
           way as for the other show commands.

SSCCHHEEDDUULLEE PPAACCKKAAGGEESS FFOORR IINNSSTTAALLLL,, RREEMMOOVVEE AANNDD PPUURRGGEE
       Some front-ends like aapptt--ggeett ddsseelleecctt--uuppggrraaddee can be used to apply
       previously scheduled changes to the install state of packages. Such
       changes can be scheduled with the iinnssttaallll, rreemmoovvee (also known as
       ddeeiinnssttaallll) and ppuurrggee commands. Packages with a specific selection can
       be displayed with sshhoowwiinnssttaallll, sshhoowwrreemmoovvee and sshhoowwppuurrggee respectively.
       More information about these so called dpkg selections can be found in
       ddppkkgg(1).

